{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Recover the full text behind a UI-clipped tool cell by pulling it from the LLM capture store. The chat/agentloop renderer clamps long tool output to a fixed prefix and appends \"…[N chars clipped]\"; the same output was captured verbatim by chat_llm's seam when LLM_CAPTURE=on, so the visible fragment is an exact prefix of the captured content. Pass that visible fragment (without the trailing marker); this scans the day's capture rows newest-first and returns {status, id, full, clipped_chars} for the first captured message that starts with it. Gated exactly like the capture seam: LLM_CAPTURE absent or not \"on\" answers status err, so the front-end can probe cheaply and hide the expander when there is nothing to pull from.","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;","params":[{"desc":"The visible (clipped) text of the cell, without the trailing …[N chars clipped] marker. Matched as an exact prefix against captured content.","name":"fragment","type":"String"}],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"pzrpnp1a0b6e1cc06q9d","readers":[],"time":1789774676363,"username":"system","writers":[]}